From 39cf81654589fd2386d4da666600e4dd11de2477 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:18:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): engage cutter compensation in G17, never in a
 stale G18/G19

A G41/G42/G40 block that followed an XZ/YZ arc was written while
G18/G19 was still modal, so the control compensated in that plane
instead of XY. The Fanuc, Haas, Mazak and Siemens 840D posts now state
G17 on the comp block when the modal plane is not 17, and refuse by
name an XZ/YZ arc while compensation is engaged (no plane switch under
comp). Programs that never leave G17 post byte-identically.

Pinned by crates/post/tests/comp_plane.rs.

Fixes #391

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
